{{!-- First-party page written for Volta (Qompass AI, 2026). --}}
{{#> layout }}
  <h2>{{ text "About Volta" }}</h2>

  <p>
    Volta is an OpenPGP keyserver operated by Qompass AI. It supports the
    distribution and discovery of OpenPGP public keys: anyone can look up
    a key by fingerprint, key ID, or email address, and key owners can
    publish their key and manage which of their addresses are listed.
  </p>

  <p>
    Addresses are only published after the owner has verified control of
    the address through a confirmation email, and listings can be removed
    again at any time from the <a href="/manage">manage page</a>. Volta is
    derived from the Hagrid keyserver software that powers
    keys.openpgp.org, and is developed in the open at
    <a href="https://github.com/qompassai/volta/">github.com/qompassai/volta</a>.
  </p>
{{/layout}}
